{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The loops' tav.</b> The sign of the feminine, and one is לולה, and it comes under the alef of ה\"ה (the הא). Some say that from this root (comes) הרה ללת (1 Samuel 4:19)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "The phrase 'under the alef of ה\"ה' refers to the word האה in the verse; Ibn Ezra explains that the tav suffix on לולאות replaces the alef that would appear in the masculine form."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:46.743760528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}